As it turns out, lift is greater than 1.0. This could give us some confidence that the association rule we recommended did not arise by random chance.

Note: LIFT is calculated as a ratio and equals to Support(X&Y)/(Support(X)*Support(Y)) and has the threshold of determining good rules at 1.0; LEVERAGE is calculated as a difference and equals to Support(X&Y) - (Support(X)*Support(Y)) and has the threshold of determining good rules at 0.0

